---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const base='/equipment/01-04/';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Connectomics console · synthetic tile tracing" description="Trace a synthetic label across two registered tiles and verify that its world coordinates and ID stay the same at two display resolutions." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment cc"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/01-04/">← Equipment 01-04</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#cc-evidence">References and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">01-04 · VOLUME REGISTRATION / FIRST PASS</span><h2>Connectomics console</h2><p>Trace a small synthetic shape across two adjacent tiles. Switch display resolution while keeping the same world point, and check which tile, index, and segment the viewer resolves.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>Nominal workstation</h3><div id="cc-view" aria-label="Orbitable workstation with live slice and provenance screens, turquoise trackball and amber annotation button"></div><div class="bar"><button data-cc-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-cc-view="screens">Monitors</button><button data-cc-view="controls">Controls</button></div><p id="cc-ready" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p>Drag to orbit and scroll or pinch to zoom. The turquoise trackball toggles scale; the amber annotation key saves the current point. These actions match the form controls.</p></section>
<section><h3>Registered synthetic volume</h3><canvas id="cc-map" width="720" height="470" aria-label="XY slice showing left and right tiles, a dashed seam and a point cursor"></canvas><div class="fields"><label>Native Z slice index (0–7)<input id="cc-slice" type="range" min="0" max="7" step="1" value="4"/></label><label>Import synthetic fixture JSON<input id="cc-input" type="file" accept=".json,application/json"/></label></div><div class="bar"><button id="cc-demo" class="primary">Trace across the seam</button><button id="cc-zoom">Show 2× coarse</button><button id="cc-add">Add point at cursor</button><button id="cc-clear">Clear trace</button><button id="cc-reload">Restore example</button></div><p id="cc-status" aria-live="polite">Click the slice to select a cell center or run the three-node seam example.</p><output id="cc-details"></output></section></div>
<section><h3>Annotation record</h3><ol id="cc-history"></ol><div class="bar"><button id="cc-export">Export selection and trace JSON</button></div><p>Exports are local and preserve volume ID, volume revision, exact world positions, segment labels, trace links and edit history. Do not load human, animal, or patient data; this exercise is intended for tiny synthetic fixtures only.</p></section>
<section id="cc-evidence"><h3>Geometry, algorithm and evidence</h3>
<p>This is an original workstation, not a vendor system or a reproduction of a laboratory. Desk and monitor dimensions are original nominal design values. The volume and pixel intensities are generated from abstract shapes. They are not electron microscopy, anatomy, inferred connectivity or experimental data.</p>
<div class="grid"><figure><img src={base+'front.webp'} width="650" height="450" loading="lazy" alt="Original front render of dual-monitor workstation on an ivory desktop"/><figcaption>Original overall render (not a photo): nominal 1.55 × 0.74 m desktop and two display panels. Active screen textures are drawn by the simulator.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={base+'controls.webp'} width="650" height="450" loading="lazy" alt="Original controls rendering showing a turquoise trackball, keyboard and amber annotation key"/><figcaption>Original control close-up: named turquoise <code>zoom_trackball</code> and amber <code>annotation_key</code> are available to a future XR client.</figcaption></figure></div>
<p><a href="https://neuroglancer-docs.web.app/datasource/precomputed/volume.html">Neuroglancer Precomputed volume specification</a> motivates XYZ dimensions, nanometer resolutions and half-open chunk bounds; <a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41592-024-02426-z">CAVE versioning paper</a> motivates retaining annotation provenance; <a href="https://imagej.github.io/imaging/z-functions">ImageJ slice and orthogonal-view guide</a> motivates the slice interaction. The local JSON fixture is not a Precomputed, CAVE, ImageJ or FIJI file format, and no external datasets are requested.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Check or parameter</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual / meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Native voxel size / volume shape</td><td>8 × 8 × 40 nm / 16 × 12 × 8 voxels</td><td>Two equal X tiles, x-fastest arrays. Coarse display uses 16 × 16 × 80 nm.</td></tr>
<tr><td>World seam and ownership</td><td>[1064, −148, 680] nm; right tile; segment 17 at both levels</td><td>Native [8,6,4], coarse [4,3,2]. World coordinate and label exactly unchanged.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Outside volume and unrelated segment</td><td>Reject right exclusive boundary and reject trace link to label 52</td><td>Both fail without changing annotations, as expected.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Nominal desk width</td><td>1.55 m</td><td>1.55 m in GLB; absolute tolerance 0.00001 m, not a physical measurement.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>For each axis, <code>index = floor((world − origin) / (basePitch × 2^level))</code>. Both levels share the same lower-corner origin. An exact boundary belongs to the right half-open tile. Coarse signal pixels average eight native voxels; labels use the modal class, breaking ties toward the smaller ID including background. A coarse rendering can therefore obscure small labels. Points can only be added when native and display labels agree and the selected label matches the current trace. Indexing is axis aligned only, without rotation or nonlinear warps.</p>
<p><a href={base+'tiny-volume.json'} download>Synthetic volume input</a> · <a href={base+'example-annotation.json'}>Output schema/example</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'reference-cases.json'}>Locked reference cases</a> · <a href={base+'connectomics-console.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender generator</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a>. No headset, external volume streaming or downstream tool integration is claimed.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/01-04/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.cc{max-width:76rem}.cc .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.1rem}.cc section{border-top:1px solid var(--border);margin:.8rem 0;padding:.8rem 0;min-width:0}.cc .bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.45rem;margin:.55rem 0}.cc .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.5rem}.cc label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.2rem;font-size:.93rem}.cc input,.cc button{font:inherit;min-width:0;max-width:100%;min-height:2.4em;padding:.34em .52em;color:var(--text);background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.13rem}.cc button{cursor:pointer}.cc .primary{color:white;background:#245350}.cc #cc-view{height:clamp(270px,34vw,450px);background:#d9dddf;touch-action:none}.cc #cc-view :global(canvas){width:100%;height:100%;display:block}.cc #cc-map,.cc img{width:100%;height:auto}.cc #cc-map{cursor:crosshair}.cc #cc-details{white-space:pre-line;font-family:monospace;display:block}.cc #cc-status.error{color:#a54a34}.cc .scroll{overflow:auto}.cc table{font-size:.89rem;border-collapse:collapse}.cc td,.cc th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-align:left;padding:.45rem}.cc figure{margin:.8rem 0}@media(max-width:800px){.cc .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
